{"database":{"advisory-count":1555,"last-commit":"55e1c3dfbd834237a05bbbf7b50ba3b5be27b662","last-updated":"2026-11-21T10:28:03+01:00"},"lockfile":{"dependency-count":369},"settings":{"target_arch":[],"target_os":[],"severity":null,"ignore":[],"informational_warnings":["unmaintained","unsound","notice"]},"vulnerabilities":{"found":true,"count":2,"list":[{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0385","package":"ctutils","title":"Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons","description":"## Summary\n\nThe `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned\ninteger size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and\ntherefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate\nthat's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.\n\nIn releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could\ninclude a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this\nrelease and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.\n\nAdditionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and\nintended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.\nThis has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions\nfor such targets.\n\n## Impact\n\nBranch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via\ncovert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.\n\n## Resolution\n\nThis has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,\nwhich in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that\nthis resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety\nof target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs\nautomatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.","date":"2026-10-23","aliases":[],"related":["RUSTSEC-2026-0003"],"collection":"crates","categories":["crypto-failure"],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC-BY-4.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=0.4.4"],"unaffected":[]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"ctutils","version":"0.4.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"03bb0e1cc970d482d121d9a1744999169b69a07470b3d644a7894e53fcaf4574","dependencies":[{"name":"cmov","version":"0.5.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}},{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0384","package":"tokio","title":"Race condition in `tokio::time::Interval` on Tokio v1.54.0","description":"## Summary\n\nOn the multi-threaded runtime, there is a race condition between `Interval::poll_tick` and the runtime's time driver.\n\nThis affects `Interval` only. `Sleep` and `Timeout` are **not** affected.\n\n## Details\n\nIn Tokio v1.54.0, a race condition between `tokio::time::Interval::poll_tick` (including `.tick().await`) and the runtime time driver can drop an internal timer entry without synchronizing with the driver thread that is firing it. This causes a data race and use-after-free on the timer's waker and task state in safe Rust, leading to assertion panics, task reference-count corruption, or heap memory corruption.\n\nThis bug was introduced by https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8458, and it was fixed by https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8692.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis may lead to crashes and use-after-frees in applications using `Interval` on a multi-threaded runtime.\n\nSince this issue is known to lead to crashes in production systems, the v1.54.0 release of Tokio has been yanked.\n\n## Credits\n\nThank you to [creepycode](https://github.com/ByteZ1337) and [carabistouille](https://github.com/carabistouflette) for reporting this privately using the procedure outlined in our security policy. They both reported the issue independently of each other.","date":"2026-10-21","aliases":["CVE-2026-115567","GHSA-5wjr-9356-4wc8"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["memory-corruption","thread-safety"],"keywords":["race condition","use-after-free"],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8692","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=1.54.1"],"unaffected":["<1.54.0"]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"tokio","version":"1.54.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"a0c168a474b95bfecfe908a65d4bdffc523144b649a74c09c286afb35d53e0bc","dependencies":[{"name":"bytes","version":"1.12.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.191","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"mio","version":"1.2.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"pin-project-lite","version":"0.2.17","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"signal-hook-registry","version":"1.4.8","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"socket2","version":"0.6.5","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"tokio-macros","version":"2.7.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"windows-sys","version":"0.61.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}}]},"warnings":{"unmaintained":[{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"atomic-polyfill","version":"1.0.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"8cf2bce30dfe09ef0bfaef228b9d414faaf7e563035494d7fe092dba54b300f4","dependencies":[{"name":"critical-section","version":"1.2.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2023-0089","package":"atomic-polyfill","title":"atomic-polyfill is unmaintained","description":"The author has archived the GitHub repository and mentions deprecation in\nproject's\n[README](https://github.com/embassy-rs/atomic-polyfill/blob/48e55c166684f37af0b00fbee5a0809b1a2bae8e/README.md).\n\n## Possible alternatives\n\n * [portable-atomic](https://crates.io/crates/portable-atomic)","date":"2023-07-11","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/embassy-rs/atomic-polyfill/commit/48e55c166684f37af0b00fbee5a0809b1a2bae8e","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"chrono","version":"0.4.45","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"1aa79e62e7697b8e29b513a68abacf485adcd1fe8284a4316c5ae868e6633327","dependencies":[{"name":"iana-time-zone","version":"0.1.65","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"num-traits","version":"0.2.19","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"serde","version":"1.0.229","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"windows-link","version":"0.2.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0543","package":"chrono","title":"chrono is unmaintained","description":"The chrono crate is unmaintained; all versions are affected.\n\nRecommended alternatives:\n\n- [jiff](https://crates.io/crates/jiff)\n- [time](https://crates.io/crates/time)","date":"2026-09-14","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/chronotope/chrono/issues/1768","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"pa